=== p2-windows · W7 · page:charging/TeslaChargingSessions (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:charging/TeslaChargingSessions   kind=page   web route=/tesla-charging-sessions
Web source  : web/src/features/charging/pages/TeslaChargingSessionsPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7
  ApiLogsPage / VehicleCostPage do. The generated prompt's idealized "TeslaChargingSessionsPage.xaml +
  ViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Charging" is mapped onto these real conventions. The surface registers
  itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("TeslaChargingSessions") in ShellWindow.xaml.cs.
- Data binding (ADR-004): the three manifest data sources are bound through the generated OpenAPI contract client
  (TeslaChargingSessionsPage.Source.cs / TeslaChargingSessionsClientFeed) — useTeslaChargingSessions →
  get_api_v1_tesla_charging_sessions (GET /tesla/charging/sessions/, snake_case `vin` query, omitted for "All
  Vehicles"); useVehicles → get_api_v1_vehicles (GET /vehicles/); useRefreshTeslaChargingSessions →
  post_api_v1_tesla_charging_sessions_refresh (POST /tesla/charging/sessions/refresh, `vin` query). All three
  operation ids are confirmed present in apps/windows/Generated/Api/ApiEndpoints.cs. No HTTP touches the view; the
  ViewModel reads through the injected ITeslaChargingSessionsFeed (default EmptyTeslaChargingSessionsFeed = empty
  state). A refresh that returns HTTP 403 surfaces as ApiException(StatusCode=403) → the distinct "business account
  required" note (web is403); other failures are non-fatal to the page and keep the existing data.
- Envelope/SI: TeslaChargingSessionsSnapshot.FromJson unwraps the platform httputil.Respond {data:{sessions,summary}}
  envelope before reading the snake_case sessions[]/summary so the wire shape round-trips losslessly. Energy is read
  as SI watt-hours and converted ONLY at the display boundary: the Total-Energy card via the shared
  UnitFormatters.FormatEnergy(total_wh, units) and the table Energy(kWh) column via
  UnitConverters.EnergyFromSi(wh, Kwh) + NumberFormatting (web convertEnergyFromSI(_, 'kWh')). Cost/rate format
  through ScalarFormatters.FormatCurrency (web formatCurrency / formatCurrencyValue); the duration column reproduces
  web formatDurationSeconds; the monthly chart reproduces web buildMonthlyCost (YYYY-MM bucket, summed cost, sorted).
- Maps=0 for this unit (the slippy map is the SEPARATE parity unit feature-views/TeslaChargingSessionsMap, whose
  data source is a heavily-coupled cache-then-network pipeline). GlassPanel9 ("Session Locations") is therefore
  reproduced as the Fluent locations data region the web map plots — each geolocated session's site name + "lat, lng"
  (TeslaChargingMapPoint) in a scroller — with the web noMapData TsEmptyState when no session has coordinates. Never
  a blank region, no web pixel-cloning, and the dedicated map widget is not duplicated here.
- States (ADR-006): the web renders its regions inside PageContainer (loading/error). The native port reproduces the
  four data states as visible Fluent regions — loading -> TsStatGridSkeleton(5)+TsTableSkeleton shimmer; error ->
  TsQueryError (InfoBar-equivalent) + Retry (ActionInvoked -> RefreshAsync); success/empty content -> the info banner
  + controls bar + five TsStatCards + the monthly-cost TsChartContainer + the locations panel + the session
  TsDataTable, each region with its own empty state. The stat cards/controls render in BOTH success and empty
  (matching the web, which only swaps the chart/map/table bodies for empty states), so the user can still Refresh.
- i18n (ADR-014): all 32 manifest keys resolve through the ILocalizer facade with the verbatim web key names. 28 were
  already present in Strings/en/Resources.resw (translation.tesla_sessions.* / translation.table.bulkActions.exportCsv);
  the 4 the web page uses that the catalog lacked — tesla_sessions.businessNote, tesla_sessions.monthlyCost.aria,
  tesla_sessions.stats.cost_decimal, tesla_sessions.col.cost_decimal (the catalog still carried the older
  stats.cost / col.cost variants) — were added verbatim. No literal is hardcoded. The ar/he catalogs lag en by
  design; the app falls back to the English default via ILocalizer until translated.
- Microsoft.UI-free Model/Source/ViewModel links were added to TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj (the bare WinUI view is
  excluded — it uses Microsoft.UI). A namespace-local internal JsonReadHelpers provides null-tolerant parsing.
- Build/lint defects found + fixed in this surface's own new code (no red shipped): (1) a PRE-EXISTING build break —
  Shell/ShellWindow.xaml.cs's AutomationList PageFactory.Register lambda was missing its `return page; });`, a C#
  syntax error that cascaded into 160+ XAML-compiler WMC0001/WMC0110 + a WMC9999 internal crash across the whole app;
  repaired (the nav-registration area is in scope) so the solution compiles; (2) the app project enforces CA1859 as an
  error, so three private helpers (BuildChartSeries / BuildMapPoints / VinQuery) were given concrete return types;
  (3) the new files were normalised from CRLF to LF to satisfy dotnet format ENDOFLINE. All repaired; the app +
  solution build 0 errors and dotnet format reports 0 changes.

